WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.900
- I've heard that you
speak about co-parenting

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:03.570
and I'm doing that right now, too.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.673
It's tough.

00:00:06.168 --> 00:00:07.333
Is it harder than you thought?

00:00:08.343 --> 00:00:10.120
Is it working with you and Tristan?

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.400
I know with me and Brandon,

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.730
it's just a difficult thing
'cause we're in different places

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.350
and it's like we both
agree on the main things,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.100
but it's a hard thing
when you're not together

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.460
all the time, for me personally.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.600
Has it been hard for you?

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.840
- My parents were the most perfect example

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.360
and I was really blessed
and fortunate to have that

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:32.810
as my example, and to see
that, and even with my stepdad

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:34.450
and the integration of all of that

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:37.740
and how my dad and my stepdad
dealt with one another

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:42.380
was really just such a
beautiful thing to witness.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.530
They played golf once a week and I'm sure

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.830
that wasn't easy for my
dad, but he did it for us.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:50.860
And so, having that
really selfless example

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:51.693
was awesome for us.

00:00:51.693 --> 00:00:53.900
So, I think, with all of
us, whether it be Kourtney

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.400
and Scott or Tristan and
myself, we definitely,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.763
I try to mirror that and
always keep it about the kids,

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:03.650
but with Tristan, it's a trust thing

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:06.890
and Tristan is so great and
really trust me as a mom

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:09.360
and knows I'm always gonna
do the right thing for True.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:13.010
So, he really doesn't tell
me no, a lot of the times

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:15.960
and I'm grateful for that
because I think, as moms,

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.440
we just sort of feel like
we have the right to,

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.480
we know what we're doing with our kids.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.740
But it was funny, the other day I wanted,

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.420
True is gonna be three in April,

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.990
and I wanted to give
her her very first trim

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:30.170
and when I mean trim, like
not even half an inch,

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:32.480
I just wanted to cut
some of her baby hairs

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.320
and Tristan, I don't
think has ever told me no,

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.450
and he really freaked out by
me wanting to cut her hair.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:42.710
And I just, it was so crazy
to me how he was freaking out.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:45.700
He called my brother for my
brother to talk me out of it.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:46.533
He called my mom.

00:01:46.533 --> 00:01:48.967
I was like, "Oh my God, I
wasn't gonna give her a trim

00:01:48.967 --> 00:01:51.650
"if you," I didn't know he
was that adamant about it,

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.910
until everybody else started calling me,

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:58.910
but I didn't do it 'cause I
also have to show him that I,

00:01:58.977 --> 00:02:00.597
"Okay, if you don't
want me to do something

00:02:00.597 --> 00:02:02.490
"that badly, I'm not gonna do it."

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.880
So it's just, I think,
great with communication

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:07.380
and trust is the most important thing,

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:08.930
I think, with raising kids.

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:09.763
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:02:09.763 --> 00:02:10.596
I think you're right, too.

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:11.850
That's what Brandon and
I are focusing on, too,

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:14.450
it's like as long as you make
sure it's about the children

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:16.950
and their best interest,
then we're both on board.

